<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><document level="portable"><documentinfo><uri title="manual-numbering-true-prefix"><displaytitle>manual-numbering-true-prefix</displaytitle></uri></documentinfo><section id="title"><fragment id="title"><para>Test Case 9</para></fragment></section><section id="1"><fragment id="1"><para>Basic Word document with split configuration: document set to false.</para><para>Test of that false in document split is working, even with valid split values.</para><heading level="5" prefix="Schedule 1">Amendments</heading><heading level="2" prefix="Part 1">Main amendments of the Private Health Insurance Act 2007</heading><heading level="3" prefix="Section 1&#x9;">Private Health Insurance Act 2007</heading><para prefix="1 "> Subsections 22-15(2), (3) and (4)</para><para>Omit “mentioned in subsection (1)”, substitute “specified in subsection (1) (as affected by subsection (5A))”.</para><para prefix="2 "> After subsection 22-15(5)</para><para indent="4">Insert:</para><para>Annual adjustment of percentages</para><block label="sub"><para indent="1" prefix="(5A)">For each adjustment year, each percentage specified in subsection (1), (2) or (3) is replaced by the percentage worked out as follows:</para></block><para indent="2" prefix="(a)">for the adjustment year starting on 1 April 2014—multiply the specified percentage by the adjustment factor for the adjustment year;</para><para indent="2" prefix="(b)">for a later adjustment year—multiply the specified percentage, as worked out under this subsection for the preceding adjustment year, by the adjustment factor for the later adjustment year.</para><para prefix="(5B)" indent="1">Percentages are to be worked out under subsection (5A) to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).</para><block label="sub"><para indent="1" prefix="(5C)">The percentages worked out under subsection (5A) for an adjustment year apply in relation to premiums, or amounts in respect of premiums, that were paid, or that are payable, at any time in the adjustment year.</para></block><block label="sub"><para indent="1" prefix="5D">Each of the following is an <bold><italic>adjustment year</italic></bold>:</para></block><para indent="2" prefix="A">the period of 12 months starting on 1 April 2014;</para><para indent="2" prefix="B">the period of 12 months starting on each later 1 April.</para><block label="sub"><para indent="1" prefix="(5E)">The <bold><italic>adjustment factor </italic></bold>for an adjustment year is to be determined in accordance with the Private Health Insurance (Incentives) Rules. However, if the factor so determined for an adjustment year is more than 1, the <bold><italic>adjustment factor</italic></bold> for that year is instead taken to be 1.</para></block><para prefix="3 "> Subdivision 22-C</para><para>Repeal the Subdivision.</para><para prefix="4 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1</para><para>Insert:</para><para><bold><italic>adjustment factor</italic></bold> for an adjustment year has the meaning given by subsection 22-15(5E).</para><para><bold><italic>adjustment year</italic></bold> has the meaning given by subsection 22-15(5D).</para><para prefix="5 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>base premium</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="6 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>base premium indexation factor</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="7 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>CPI indexation factor</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="8 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>CPI index number</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="9 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>premium indexation factor</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="10 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>reference premium</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para prefix="11 "> Clause 1 of Schedule 1 (definition of <italic>weighted average ratio</italic>)</para><para>Repeal the definition.</para><para/></fragment></section></document>